# Compose UI conventions (`com/assistant/ui`)

- Jetpack Compose + Material3 only; no new XML layouts in this package tree
- Theme via `AssistantTheme` / `AssistantTokens` / `AssistantOverlayTokens` — avoid one-off magic colors in immersive/chrome
- Keep composables free of agent/LLM/VHAL imports; use `AssistantBackend` events + host contracts
- Prefer small focused composables; extract shared chrome to `ui/chrome/`, motion helpers beside the feature
- Automotive: large touch targets, glanceable type, avoid dense “dashboard” chrome on the immersive stage
- Motion should signal presence/state (enter, listening, thinking, speaking) — not decorative noise
- Tests for stage/placement contracts live under `app/src/test/java/com/assistant/ui/`
